  "final_message": "Implemented the full book library app.\n\n**Backend** (`backend/app.py`): SQLite-backed Flask API with token auth (PBKDF2 password hashing, bearer tokens), paged/searchable books, per-book reviews (one per user), rating aggregation rounded half-up to one decimal, cascading review deletion, validation errors as `{\"error\": ...}`, plus SPA static serving with deep-link fallback.\n\n**Frontend** (`frontend/src/`): React + TypeScript + Tailwind v4. Hash-free client router with search/paging, sign-in/register (auto sign-in on register), book table, book detail with reviews and rating form, add/edit forms surfacing API validation messages, and confirm-on-delete.\n\nVerified: `npm ci && npm run build` succeeds, `tsc --noEmit` clean, and API smoke tests (auth, CRUD, search/paging, review uniqueness, rating averages, 401/404/409 paths, static/deep-link serving) all pass under gunicorn on port 8000.\n\nNote: no Docker available in this sandbox, so the image itself wasn't built, but the app was run through the same gunicorn entrypoint the Dockerfile uses.",
  "final_message_truncated": false,
